 or in part by an Artificial Intelligence-based application without attribution to the application will be treated as plagiarism.","sourceUrls":["https://www.uwyo.edu/regs-policies/_files/docs/regulations-2023/uwreg2-114approved7-14-23.pdf"]},{"id":"claim:claim-uwyo-library-citing-ai-guidance","category":"tracker_addition","theme":"academic_integrity","claimId":"claim-uwyo-library-citing-ai-guidance","matchMethod":"none","newText":"UW Libraries AI Support guidance says users should cite AI tools and AI-generated outputs when quoting, paraphrasing, or incorporating AI-generated ideas into their own work.","sourceUrls":["https://uwyo.libguides.com/ai-support/cite"]},{"id":"claim:claim-uwyo-library-faculty-ai-syllabus-guidance","category":"tracker_addition","theme":"teaching","claimId":"claim-uwyo-library-faculty-ai-syllabus-guidance","matchMethod":"none","newText":"UW Libraries AI Support faculty guidance points faculty to University of Wyoming Artificial Intelligence Committee syllabus-language recommendations and provides AI-related assignment design considerations.","sourceUrls":["https://uwyo.libguides.com/ai-support/faculty-resources"]},{"id":"claim:claim-uwyo-library-student-ai-integrity-guidance","category":"tracker_addition","theme":"academic_integrity","claimId":"claim-uwyo-library-student-ai-integrity-guidance","matchMethod":"none","newText":"UW Libraries AI Support student guidance advises students to use generative AI chatbots as supplementary tools, avoid copy-pasting chatbot responses into work, and check with instructors before using AI chatbots for assignments.","sourceUrls":["https://uwyo.libguides.com/ai-support/student-resources"]},{"id":"source_added:https://uwyo.libguides.com/ai-support/cite","category":"source_update","theme":"sources","matchMethod":"source_claim_type","sourceUrls":["https://uwyo.libguides.com/ai-support/cite"]},{"id":"source_added:https://uwyo.libguides.com/ai-support/faculty-resources","category":"source_update","theme":"source